<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26475" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lībĕrātor</span></b> ,
			ōris, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				freer, deliverer, liberator</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">patriae liberatores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Phil. 1, 2, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 1,
					60</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nostri liberatores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 14, 12, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">liberator suus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 6,
					14</span></i>
			: scortorum, * <i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Pers. 3, 3, 14</span></i>.— 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">In apposition: liberator populus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					35, 18 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—So as an epithet of Jupiter (like <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζευς ἐλευθέριος</span>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">libare se liquorem illum Jovi liberatori,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 15, 64</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">16, 35</span></i>.—So  in eccl.
			Lat. freq. of God: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">refugium meum ac liberator meus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Psa. 17, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">liberator ille populi Romani animus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 1,
					56</span></i>
			.</div>
